      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. Confirming the dose doesn't change the safety problem. It's five times the labeled maximum, and I'm not aware of any indication that calls for it in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function. I also can't verify the clinical context from here. A dose this far over the maximum could cause serious harm if it's given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 10 mg once daily, or 5 mg if you want to titrate up, and you can adjust it later.\n- **Document the rationale.** If there's a specific reason for 50 mg, such as a protocol, a specialist recommendation, or a monitored setting, send me that rationale. I'd still advise discussing it with pharmacy or the attending first. I'd want that conversation to happen before I enter an order this far outside the normal range.\n- **Go through pharmacy directly.** A pharmacist or the attending can enter or co-sign a non-standard order through the hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
